Methods for preventing, identifying, recording, and reporting Diversion, Inversion,
theft, or loss, and for correcting all errors and inaccuracies in inventories. These policies
shall, at minimum, include plans for compliance with {{ref:500.105(8)}}, {{ref:500.110(9)}}, and {{ref:500.141(8)}}, if applicable;

Procedures to ensure that products purchased for consumption on-site are
distinguished from products purchased for retail sale which are not to be consumed
on-site, if applicable;

Procedures that describe infusion processes permitted by Consumers, including
procedures to prevent cross-contamination and to ensure that no infusion activities occur
by Marijuana Establishment Agents in violation of {{ref:500.141(9)(c)}};

Security procedures, including specific plans for securing entrances and that all
Marijuana and Marijuana Products are kept, sold, stored, and, if applicable, consumed,
out of plain sight and not visible from a public place;

Procedures for Social Consumption Establishments regarding transportation between
Marijuana Establishments and, if applicable, to Temporary Consumption Events, in
accordance with {{ref:500.105(13)}};

Procedures to prevent overserving Consumers, including the development of
standards, consistent with Responsible Vendor Training, for Marijuana Establishment
Agents to use to evaluate impairment;

Procedures to ensure that all Marijuana Accessories provided by the Social
Consumption Establishment used by Consumers on-site are cleaned and sanitized after
use;

Allow, encourage or permit any organized game or contest involving the competitive
or cooperative consumption of Marijuana or Marijuana Product or awarding of Marijuana
or Marijuana Products as a prize;
